vanced  than almost any observer would have  deemed possible  and together with partners we're working  to further isolate the russian  leadership and we also from a swedish  perspective want to be very constructive  in the discussions of the fifth sanction  package of sanctions  we also remain committed to support  ukraine with humanitarian financial and  military aid and sweden has already  contributed with total  10 000 anti-tank weapons to ukraine but  we have also increased humanitarian aid  to ukraine with 72 million euros  and we stand ready for further use of  the european peace facility so that we  european countries can continue to  support  ukraine we also we act in solidarity  with ukraine but also in solidarity with  our common values international law  human rights democracy and european  security order  and  the president and i agree that the  international intentional attacks on  civilian population and civilian objects  it's a war crime and the russian  violation of international law  must be investigated and those  responsible will be brought to justice  and sweden we are supporting the  international criminal criminal court  financially but also with experts  the russian  invasion of ukraine has made it even  more urgent and necessary to become  independent of russian oil and gas and  we should speed up the climate work in  order to cut our dependence  and it is clear that breaking our  dependency on fossil fuel is important  to fight climate change but also to  strengthen our common security  to do this we have to secure the supply  of renewable energy we need to expand  wind power and also recognize the  importance of new green solutions based  on bioenergy and forestry  and in doing this we create sustainable  societies with high growth more jobs  today and tomorrow  and here at stockholm executive where we  are today is just one good example how  we can become independent of foreign  russian oil and gas and at the same time  advance the green 