ard and get into  the process of applying for nato  membership um how do you feel this will  influence sweden's decision to follow  that path and  can one imagine that both finland and  sweden's applications would be  considered at the same time  well i mean there's uh there is a  process in finland in the finnish  government and in the finnish parliament  and we have very close contacts with  them  we also have a process in sweden and in  in the swedish parliament and government  i mean we have already decided in sweden  after the russia's invasion of ukraine  we have already decided to increase our  military spending to 2 percent of gdp  and speed up  uh our investments and  on top of that we have deepened our  partnership with nato uh but we're now  having discussions uh with the foreign  minister and the defense ministers with  all the parties in the swedish  parliament on making a new analysis of  the security situation for sweden right  now and what  we will find is the best way forward to  sweden of course we have very close  contact with finland and when they're  processed since  we do have a close cooperation in many  areas including in the defense area  i got a question to president from the  lion  about sanctions would you accept or even  welcome if sweden stops importing gas  and oil from russia  without awaiting a  decision from the european union  i think we have been  very successful in the last 44 days  by being united and moving forward  together as one union  after the invasion on day two four and  six we  presented the first three packages of  sanctions now today it's the fifth  package  behind these packages is and tremendous  excellent work  of  combining the knowledge from the  different member states and our goal to  severely impact negatively the russian  economy and the russian financial sector  so my plea is always that we move  forward together  and it's worth  really to coordinate among the member  states because then the power of the  sa